 "headline": "Chelsea edge West Ham 2-1 with late Jackson winner",
 "paragraphs": [
  "Chelsea came out on top 2-1 at Stamford Bridge, thanks to a late goal from Nicolas Jackson. West Ham struck first in the 11th minute when Mohammed Kudus finished a pass from Emerson. Chelsea hit back before half-time, as Enzo Fernández scored in the 36th minute with Jackson providing the assist.",
  "The hosts kept pushing for a winner, and in the 79th minute Jackson turned provider and then scorer. He got the goal himself after a pass from Enzo Fernández, and that was the difference. Chelsea finished with 19 shots, 10 of them on target, while West Ham managed 7 shots and 3 on target. Lucas Paquetá gave West Ham their brightest moments, with a big chance in the 30th minute that carried an xG of 0.718.",
  "Chelsea's Malo Gusto picked up four yellow cards, in the 38th, 41st, 56th and 74th minutes, which is a lot of trouble for one player. West Ham's Maximilian Kilman was also booked in the 79th minute. In the end, Chelsea's pressure paid off and they took all three points."
